This plugin is a modified version of E:/Projects/LazyBot/plugins/qq_jrrp,
which in turn ports the upstream plugin. The original notices are retained
in the adapted Python modules. The six source files reviewed for this port
were __init__.py, fortune.py, storage.py, messages.py, keyboard.py and
panels.py. All source for this BotCraft version is included in qq_jrrp/;
no original data files are required or distributed.

2026-10-01 modifications: NoneBot support, non-numeric QQ OpenID seeds,
native QQ Markdown, command keyboards, typed atomic JSON persistence and
owner-only withdrawal.
2026-10-05 modifications: BotCraft directory plugin and public QQ API,
group/C2C exact Chinese triggers, translated user-visible output,
stdlib storage validation, no reference replies and native help registration
instead of the direct panels HTTP implementation. Language files now use the
native root lang/ convention for automatic directory and packed-plugin loading;
message templates and nested Markdown translations are evaluated on sending.
2026-10-08 modifications: separate command handlers, triple-quoted submissions,
persistent submission UUIDs and migration of composite senders to official user IDs.
Withdrawal now targets a submission UUID, checks author ownership or permission
level 2, and exposes unrestricted withdrawal buttons only after successful posts.

